Z||000000||Fiero*101||11-26-2001||09:58 PM||||I know the last post was on running bad in cold weather which makes sence but...<P>Is mine the only one that runs crappy in Warm weather?<BR>I dont know how or why but my car will start with one turn of the key and no gas pedal when its cold or its cold out.<BR>BUt when its warm or warm out it takes a few gas peddal pushes and a few tries to start it then i have to wait for it to get some what warm or it will stall when i put it in gear.<BR>So any body have any ideas why my car is like this?<BR>Oh and i just got a tune up not more then a Month ago.<BR>So if its not the plugs or wires or any of that what else would make my car run like crap? In warm weather  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>oh and once again not even a month ago i tightend my Alt belt and its sqealing again any way of tighting that so it WONT squeal after a month of peace from it?<BR>Thanks for your time  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Fiero*101<P>------------------<BR>Fiero*101<BR>Gold 86 SE 2M6<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mycar101.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||fropuff||11-27-2001||06:59 PM||||...Just moving this to the top for you.  Hope you can find out what's wrong.||||reg||1
Z||000002||avengador1||11-27-2001||07:14 PM||||What all was replaced when they did the "tuneup"?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||johnt671||11-27-2001||07:18 PM||||There's a bunch of stuff that will make a car run bad, but I can't really come up with anything other than a bad temp sensor causing the car to run rich.  Would run ok until it got warm.  Post some more details any mabye some can help.||||reg||1
Z||000004||lou||11-27-2001||07:26 PM||||Did the tune up include moving the distributor timing? Or replacing the ignition cables? It sounds like bad timing or improper firing sequence is your problem.  You should not have to push or pump the gas pedal to start the car.  Also if you have nought a new alternator belt and it still squeals even thought it is tight then you need a new belt but this time get a different brand. I have found that some of the 5 grove belts have thinner grooves than others and therefor squeal.<p>[This message has been edited by lou (edited 11-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Old Lar||11-27-2001||08:12 PM||||Sqealing belts usually mean worn belts.  When were they replaced last?  Check to see if any codes are present.||||reg||1
Z||000006||ITB 2M4||11-27-2001||09:41 PM||||Just something for your future info, the car is fuel injected, and needs no pumping of the gas pedal at all.  No fuel will go through the fuel injector when you do this.<P>------------------<BR>SCCA ITB '84 Fiero 2M4||||reg||1
Z||000007||GTDude||11-27-2001||09:54 PM||||I'm with Lar....sounds like a temp sensor problem.  V6 or 4cyl?||||reg||1
