Z||000009||Rumor||11-27-2001||11:02 PM||||I saw a BIG article on this problem, I will try to dig it up for ya -<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||WKDFIRO||11-27-2001||11:43 PM||||With any warm temperature engine problem, I would suspect an electrical ignition component. Heat really starts wrecking havoc on old electrical components. Sometimes difficult starting is just a hint of something getting ready to give up. <P>Most tuneups by people who aren't familiar with Fieros seem to forget the pick-up coil all together. The cap/rotor, and coil etc. are easy to replace but I would take off the cap and check to see if the PU coil has been changed.<P>Good luck!||||reg||2
Z||000011||87GTZ34||11-27-2001||11:44 PM||||Quick starting when cold but needs time when warm... hmmm...   Well, I would start by checking the 'leak down' of the injectors.  Get a fuel pressure gauge and with the car cold, turn the key on so the fuel pump runs then shuts off.  Turn the key off for 10 seconds and repeat.  Now, watch the fuel pressure gauge and see how much pressure drops over 1 min, 2 min, 5 min, 10 min, 30 min.  It should only drop a couple of lbs/inXin per 10 to 20 minutes.  If it drops rapidly the fuel most likely is leaking through the injectors into the runners causing a flooding condition which must be pumped out (when warm) to start.  You should also repeat the test after the car is fully warmed up (driven for 30 - 60 minutes).  This is because the leakdown rate may vary when the injectors are hot.  GL and LMK what your findings are.  From there I may have a few more diagnostic test for you.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Fiero*101||11-27-2001||11:48 PM||||Damn i was hoping it was going to be somthing easy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>hahah<P>Ok this temp sensor where is it?<BR>And my mechanic knows alot about the Fiero and it was running great after i got it back but now its starting to act up on me<BR>and its a v6 86 SE<P>How do you look to see if the coil was changed? How do you check to see if the timing is right?<P>Thanks for your help evry body <BR>Greatly aprecated it<P>------------------<BR>Fiero*101<BR>Gold 86 SE 2M6<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mycar101.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000013||tesmith66||11-28-2001||01:07 PM||||As far as the alt belt goes, the aluminum bracket on the V6 is designed poorly and will crack and flex enought to make the belt squeal. I'm on my second one and it is cracked. I bought a new one at a dealer 4 years ago for only $26. I also saw a welded steel one on the net a while back, but have not seen it lately...<BR><P>------------------<BR>Timothy E. Smith<BR>1986 SE V6<BR>1984 Coupe||||reg||6
